 lie to you? On social preferences and lying aversion","a":["Sjaak Hurkens","Navin Kartik"],"y":2009,"c":"pub","j":"Experimental Economics","v":"12","i":"2","p":"180-192","r":45,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10683-008-9208-2","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1007/s10683-008-9208-2"},{"t":"A retail benchmarking approach to efficient two‐way access pricing: no termination‐based price discrimination†","a":["Doh‐Shin Jeon","Sjaak Hurkens"],"y":2008,"c":"pub","j":"RAND Journal of Economics","v":"39","i":"3","p":"822-849","r":28,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1756-2171.2008.00040.x","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1111/j.1756-2171.2008.00040.x"},{"t":"Endogenous private information structures","a":["Sjaak Hurkens","Nir Vulkan"],"y":2006,"c":"pub","j":"European Economic Review","v":"50","i":"1","p":"35-54","r":51,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroecorev.2004.09.007","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1016/j.euroecorev.2004.09.007"},{"t":"Endogenous price leadership","a":["Eric van Damme","Sjaak Hurkens"],"y":2004,"c":"pub","j":"Games and Economic Behavior","v":"47","i":"2","p":"404-420","r":17,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geb.2004.01.003","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1016/j.geb.2004.01.003"},{"t":"Free entry does not imply zero profits","a":["Sjaak Hurkens","Nir Vulkan"],"y":2003,"c":"pub","j":"Economics Letters","v":"81","i":"3","p":"285-290","r":74,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0165-1765(03)00194-0","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1016/s0165-1765(03)00194-0"},{"t":"On Forward Induction and Evolutionary and Strategic Stability","a":["Esther Hauk","Sjaak Hurkens"],"y":2002,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Economic Theory","v":"106","i":"1","p":"66-90","r":15,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1006/jeth.2001.2856","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1006/jeth.2001.2856"},{"t":"Secret information acquisition in Cournot markets","a":["Esther Hauk","Sjaak Hurkens"],"y":2001,"c":"pub","j":"Economic Theory","v":"18","i":"3","p":"661-681","r":53,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1007/pl00004205","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1007/pl00004205"},{"t":"Information acquisition and entry"